              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<p>A Maruti Suzuki A-Star spotted near Kreneng Market. Back in 2012-13, Suzuki Indomobil imported dozens of Indian-manufactured Maruti Suzuki A-Stars to Indonesia as test car, before LCGC segment become available. Eventually they picked up Wagon R over the Indian-made ones, and all A-Stars already bought by Suzuki Indomobil are now owned by dealers themselves.\n</p><p>Sumber:\n</p>\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://indianautosblog.com/2013/05/maruti-a-star-spotted-in-jakarta-78010\">1</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://otomotifnet.com/Mobil/News-Apm/Yaah-A-Star-Bukan-Mobil-Murah-Suzuki-Di-Indonesia\">2</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://oto.detik.com/mobil/2580137/suzuki-a-star-tidak-untuk-indonesia\">3</a>",
